C LB-oota
"Out-of-thin-air load buffering. C11 relaxed atomics permit r1=r2=42 (the
 standard fails to forbid it). herd cannot *exhibit* OOTA executions, so it
 reports Never here; the permission is a property of the C11 axioms, not of
 what herd enumerates. See the README and the MoRDor (.lit) companion."
{ int x=0; int y=0; }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(y,r1,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  int r2 = atomic_load_explicit(y,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(x,r2,memory_order_relaxed);
}
exists (0:r1=42 /\ 1:r2=42)
